   {
    "type": "html",
    "html": "<section class=\"sec bg-parch\"><div class=\"container cols c-1-1 items-center\">\n  <div class=\"feature reveal-left\"><span class=\"ring\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"frame img-zoom\"><img src=\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/50630/pexels-photo-50630.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1600\" alt=\"A guest looking out over Marrakech at dusk from a private terrace\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div><div class=\"badge\"><b>40 min</b><span>From the medina to the Agafay desert.</span></div></div>\n  <div><p class=\"eyebrow\">Why Marrakech</p><h2 class=\"h2 big\">Easy to reach. <span class=\"it\">Hard to forget.</span></h2><p class=\"lead\">Marrakech has the widest choice of palace hotels and private riads in the country, and the desert and the Atlas within an hour. It is where most of our journeys begin — and where our atelier is.</p>\n  <ol class=\"nlist\"><li class=\"reveal\" style=\"transition-delay:0ms\"><span class=\"n\">01</span><div><h3>The medina and the souks.</h3><p>Explored privately, or after hours with an artisan guide.</p></div></li><li class=\"reveal\" style=\"transition-delay:80ms\"><span class=\"n\">02</span><div><h3>Palaces and gardens.</h3><p>Historic venues available for private dinners and receptions.</p></div></li><li class=\"reveal\" style=\"transition-delay:160ms\"><span class=\"n\">03</span><div><h3>Rooftops at dusk.</h3><p>Terraces with views to the Koutoubia and the mountains.</p></div></li><li class=\"reveal\" style=\"transition-delay:240ms\"><span class=\"n\">04</span><div><h3>The Palmeraie and Agafay.</h3><p>Balloon flights and desert camps on the city’s edge.</p></div></li></ol></div>\n</div></section>"
   },
   {
    "type": "html",
    "html": "<section class=\"sec bg-ivory\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"head-row\"><div class=\"reveal\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Houses we use</p><h2 class=\"h2 big\">Where to <span class=\"it\">stay.</span></h2></div></div><div class=\"grid mt-14\" style=\"gap:1.5rem\"><article class=\"scard lift reveal\" style=\"transition-delay:0ms\"><div class=\"pic img-zoom\"><img src=\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/7391720/pexels-photo-7391720.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1600\" alt=\"Riad lounge with carved plaster and lantern light\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div><div class=\"txt\"><span class=\"kicker\">Marrakech</span><h3>Royal Mansour Marrakech</h3><p>A city of private riads inside the walls — commissioned for heads of state, now yours for a week.</p></div></article><article class=\"scard lift reveal\" style=\"transition-delay:80ms\"><div class=\"pic img-zoom\"><img src=\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/27945049/pexels-photo-27945049.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1600\" alt=\"Palace courtyard with fountain and arches\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div><div class=\"txt\"><span class=\"kicker\">Marrakech</span><h3>La Mamounia</h3><p>The legendary palace garden. Churchill painted here. You will understand why by the second breakfast.</p></div></article></div></div></section>"
   },
